    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (78.26) and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.75) anchoring the offense. Both benefit significantly from facing Tomoyuki Sugano, whose 4.73 xERA signals a prime opportunity for this duo to exploit. **Trea Turner**\u2019s value is further buoyed by his leadoff spot, providing maximum opportunities for stolen bases, our highest priority category. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** (72.28) remains a must-start despite a negative platoon split against Andrew Abbott, as his elite 0.428 xwOBA effectively renders the matchup context secondary. **Junior Caminero** (62.32) and **Dillon Dingler** (60.86) also project as strong starts, with **Dillon Dingler** benefiting from a robust 14% dynamic platoon boost against Noah Cameron.\n\nRegarding roster management, the final spot in our lineup was a close call between **Luke Raley** and the bench option **Chase Meidroth**. Ultimately, **Chase Meidroth** (37.95) was excluded due to the daunting task of facing Logan Gilbert; while **Chase Meidroth** offers decent base utility, the 19% penalty applied for Gilbert's elite SP skill dropped him well below our viability floor. We continue to monitor the status of **Christian Yelich** and **Lars Nootbaar**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, while **Zac Veen** remains unavailable due to his current assignment in the minors.\n\nA critical risk factor today is the reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; should managers shuffle the batting order, the projected efficiency scores for players like **Gary Sanchez** (51.99) and **Hyeseong Kim** (54.79) could fluctuate, particularly given their dependence on order-based modifiers. Furthermore, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (50.51) faces the toughest matchup of the day against Jacob deGrom. While his dynamic platoon edge against the righty provides a slight buffer, the steep 19% SP skill penalty necessitates a cautious outlook for his counting stats, though his elite stolen base potential keeps him marginally above our bench threshold.",
